---
import GuideArticleLayout from '../../layouts/GuideArticleLayout.astro';
---

<GuideArticleLayout 
	title="Weeklist" 
	description="Learn how to plan your week and sync tasks to the timer."
>
	<section class="space-y-4">
		<h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-[1.65rem] font-semibold text-zinc-950 dark:text-zinc-50 tracking-tight">Purpose</h2>
		<p class="text-base sm:text-[16px] text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
			A relative 14-day planner (Current Week and Next Week) to organize up to 3 priority tasks per day.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="space-y-4">
		<h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-[1.65rem] font-semibold text-zinc-950 dark:text-zinc-50 tracking-tight">Adding &amp; Sending</h2>
		<p class="text-base sm:text-[16px] text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
			Type a task and click the <code class="font-mono text-zinc-800 dark:text-zinc-200">+</code> button. Click <code class="font-mono text-zinc-800 dark:text-zinc-200">▶</code> to send a single task to the On Screen Timer, or <code class="font-mono text-zinc-800 dark:text-zinc-200">→</code> to send all tasks for that day.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="space-y-4">
		<h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-[1.65rem] font-semibold text-zinc-950 dark:text-zinc-50 tracking-tight">Status Dots</h2>
		<p class="text-base sm:text-[16px] text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
			Red means pending/unsent. Yellow means it is currently active in the Timer. Green means it is completed.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="space-y-4">
		<h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-[1.65rem] font-semibold text-zinc-950 dark:text-zinc-50 tracking-tight">Swap Weeks</h2>
		<p class="text-base sm:text-[16px] text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
			Click <code class="font-mono text-zinc-800 dark:text-zinc-200">⇄ Swap Weeks</code> to rotate your current and next week arrays.
		</p>
	</section>
</GuideArticleLayout>
